#######
# Setup
#######

($n, $d) = random_coprime([-10..-1],[2..10]);
Context("Fraction");
$a = Fraction($n,$d);
$ans = 1/$a;

#############################
# Exercise Group Introduction
#############################

BEGIN_PGML
Find the indicated inverse.

END_PGML

######
# Body
######

BEGIN_PGML
Multiplicative inverse of [`[$a]\text{.}`]

[_]{$ans}{5}

END_PGML

##########
# Solution
##########

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
The multiplicative inverse of a negative number will still be negative. The multiplicative inverse of fraction swaps the numerator and denominator. So here the multiplicative inverse of [`[$a]`] is [`[$ans]\text{.}`]

END_PGML_SOLUTION

